# Git Branch Naming

When creating branches, do NOT use the `cursor/<name>` prefix. Use a plain, descriptive branch name instead.

```bash
# ❌ BAD
git checkout -b cursor/add-login-form

# ✅ GOOD
git checkout -b add-login-form
```

Apply the same convention when committing or pushing: branch names should never carry the `cursor/` prefix.
